# --- Mouse + gamepad additions (setup-windows.ps1) ---
weapon_fire {
   + mouse      LeftBtn
}
hardpoint2_fire {
   + mouse      RightBtn
}
pilot_glance_left {
   + mouse      MiddleBtn
}

# --- Right-hand home-row fire keys (added 2026-10-03, owner ruling) ---
# ADDITIVE: a second block for the same action is an ALTERNATIVE binding, not a
# chord. 1 and 2 keep firing as before; J and L add a right-hand way to do it.
# L, not K, for hardpoint 2: K is the radar camera here and the wheel layer types
# K for it. The swap (K = hardpoint 2, radar camera on L) is in controls/README.md.
hardpoint1_fire {
   + keyboard   J
	- Keyboard	Shift
	- Keyboard	Control
}
hardpoint2_fire {
   + keyboard   L
	- Keyboard	Shift
	- Keyboard	Control
}



# =====================================================================
#  WHEEL / JOYSTICK BUTTON TIER  (restored 2026-08-08)
#
#  WHY THIS KEEPS DISAPPEARING: the in-game controls menu REWRITES input.map
#  and silently drops bindings it does not understand. Twice now the file has
#  come back with the two ANALOG joystick lines intact (steer + throttle) and
#  every joystick BUTTON block gone - which is exactly the symptom "steering
#  and pedals and force feedback all work, but no buttons do anything".
#
#  The device is never at fault in that state: winmm still enumerates the wheel
#  with all 13 buttons, and the lint passes, because what is left IS valid -
#  there is simply nothing bound. Check `grep -i joystick input.map`: if the
#  only hits are the two axis lines, this block has been eaten again.
#
#  These are ALTERNATIVES layered on top of the keyboard/mouse bindings above -
#  additive, nothing removed. Rollback = delete this whole block.
#  Button numbers are the wheel's winmm indices; identify yours with
#  tools\ffb\ffb-buttons.ps1 and edit to taste.
# =====================================================================

#  SUPERSEDED 2026-08-08 - this tier has been REMOVED, deliberately.
#
#  Wheel buttons are owned by i76-remap.ahk, which emits the engine's stock
#  KEYS for them. That is the documented design (docs/WHEEL-T300.md) and it
#  buys a shift layer: ~27 actions from 13 buttons, where a native binding
#  here tops out at one action per button and cannot be shifted at all.
#
#  Binding them in BOTH places double-fires. Measured with the tier present:
#  button 1 fired weapon_fire here AND hardpoint2 via AHK - two weapon
#  effects from one press, which is the exact pattern that crashed
#  I7_SFRCE.DLL on 2026-08-01. Button 3 cycled weapons twice per press.
#
#  If wheel buttons go dead, the cause is almost certainly that _ahk\i76-remap.ahk
#  is missing or STALE - not that this block is absent. Check it has a
#  gWheelBase table (`grep gWheelBase`); a copy without one predates the wheel
#  layer entirely, which is exactly how this tier came to be added.
#
#  Previous contents preserved in input.map.pre-wheel-ahk-20260808.
